{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1278957-spells-dynamics-and-conditions","id":1278957,"title":"Spells dynamics and conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-06T06:47:07-08:00","id":1278957,"title":"Spells dynamics and conditions","content":"We all know that to &quot;hang&quot; a spell a mage requires Time 4, and to add a condition (other than time passing) to trigger that spell, another sphere must comlement the spell.<br /> But how far can a mage acomplish without Time 4? How dynamic can be an effect? Could they work like computer programming (If..Then, While, etc.)?<br /> <br /> For example, would a mage need Time 4 to cast an effect on an area to make anyone who enters sleep? As I see this works similar to a ward. Except ward doesn't make people sleep or cast any spell, just prevents the target from getting in/closer/grabbing. And wards doesn't require Time 4.<br /> Another example, if a mage wants to cast a Life spell that is constantly scanning her health condition and if (or while) she isn't in perfect health, it heals her. <br /> <br /> Note that those effects differ from a Time 4 &quot;hang&quot; spell as they are constantly &quot;running&quot; or &quot;scanning&quot; the ambient/target in order to procede and change the effect from scanning to actually doing something. So the spell is active, while a Time 4 effect is inactive until the trigger happens. <br /> Or maybe they doesn't need the trigger at all, just are constantly doing the effect. In the examples above, the area would be always making everyone sleep, and the target would be constantly healing. The thing is, while there is no one in the area, no one would sleep. And as long as there is nothing to heal, the mage is not visibily healed. This would be the same as a persistent effect like a wall of fire that is always burning ,but won't do damage unless someone pass through it.<br /> <br /> Could a mage cast a spell on someone so everytime the target curses a &quot;beep&quot; sound cones out instead of the word with just Forces and Life(to lock)?<br /> Could this be done with a Force field that activates by a command?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T07:18:05-08:00","id":1279200,"title":"","content":"I use persistent effects in the examples you provided.<br /> <br /> The censorship effect I would rule as a Forces/Mind effect (or just mind if you don't mind that the beep is done through the target speaking \u201cbeep\u201c instead of the curse).<br /> Forces 2 to alter the sound and Mind 3 to scan for cursing and to lock the Forces effect.<br /> Alternatively Mind 4 to Force the target to speak \u201cbeep\u201c instead of the intended cursing word(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T14:58:38-08:00","id":1279313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1278957-spells-dynamics-and-conditions?p=1279200#post1279200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use persistent effects in the examples you provided.<br /> <br /> The censorship effect I would rule as a Forces/Mind effect (or just mind if you don't mind that the beep is done through the target speaking \u201cbeep\u201c instead of the curse).<br /> Forces 2 to alter the sound and Mind 3 to scan for cursing and to lock the Forces effect.<br /> Alternatively Mind 4 to Force the target to speak \u201cbeep\u201c instead of the intended cursing word(s).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see. Then you agree that it is possible to set up conditions without the Time sphere. How would you describe the effect? I'd say it's a persistent effect that is constantly checking what the target is about to say and is activated when she says one of the &quot;pre programed&quot; words. But this would mean that mage indeed can set conditions to their effects, when it is cast upon something/someone/someplace...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T03:40:48-08:00","id":1279445,"title":"","content":"I think that storing / hanging Effects for later use should require Time Magick of the same level as the Effect that is stored. Currently it is very nonsensical I think, as Time 4 is required to store Effects of lower levels, including very simple level 1 Effects. Also, I don't think most Paradigms would justify this easily or clearly. Level 5 Effects would require higher Time Magick than currently, but I think that they are so potent that this is justified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T04:39:40-08:00","id":1279450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1278957-spells-dynamics-and-conditions?p=1279313#post1279313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see. Then you agree that it is possible to set up conditions without the Time sphere. How would you describe the effect? I'd say it's a persistent effect that is constantly checking what the target is about to say and is activated when she says one of the &amp;quot;pre programed&amp;quot; words. But this would mean that mage indeed can set conditions to their effects, when it is cast upon something/someone/someplace...</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion pre-programmed words would be difficult. The Mind portion of the effect determines if the target is about to say \u201cbad words\u201c, so some people can get words out unaffected if said person doesn't perceive it as an act of cursing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T09:03:48-08:00","id":1279479,"title":"","content":"I see. But still, this is an example of a spell that changes it's effect according to certain condition, without using Time.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> what if the effect is not being &quot;stored&quot; nor &quot;hanged&quot; like the examples in OP? Those are just constantly running spells that change behavior according to specific conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:12:19-08:00","id":1280364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1278957-spells-dynamics-and-conditions?p=1279479#post1279479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> what if the effect is not being &quot;stored&quot; nor &quot;hanged&quot; like the examples in OP? Those are just constantly running spells that change behavior according to specific conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this can be done, but it does make me question the usefulness of the storing / hanging part of Time 4. I think it would be better if Effects could be cast with simple conditions ( maybe including time elapsed or at regular time intervals ) , pertinent to the Effect, that activate or change the Effect later. But to do so successes need to be put into duration, and maybe also additional success(es) is needed to weave the trigger change into the Effect. Time 4 would allow for more complex conditions and triggers, and for modifying on an ongoing basis time periods during which an Effect is active ; and with Time 4 the Mage wouldn't have to put successes into duration for Effects which are in passive state until activated.<br /> I will re-read the pertinent sections of the books and think about this later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T08:46:57-08:00","id":1289196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1278957-spells-dynamics-and-conditions?p=1280364#post1280364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this can be done, but it does make me question the usefulness of the storing / hanging part of Time 4. I think it would be better if Effects could be cast with simple conditions ( maybe including time elapsed or at regular time intervals ) , pertinent to the Effect, that activate or change the Effect later. But to do so successes need to be put into duration, and maybe also additional success(es) is needed to weave the trigger change into the Effect. Time 4 would allow for more complex conditions and triggers, and for modifying on an ongoing basis time periods during which an Effect is active ; and with Time 4 the Mage wouldn't have to put successes into duration for Effects which are in passive state until activated.<br /> I will re-read the pertinent sections of the books and think about this later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about this. And the only use I found for Time 4 instead of another &quot;trigger&quot; is that with Time, you don't have to spend successes on duration. <br /> Not really a good advantage since a few successes can make an effect last for days...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:28:26-08:00","id":1289205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1278957-spells-dynamics-and-conditions?p=1289196#post1289196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about this. And the only use I found for Time 4 instead of another &quot;trigger&quot; is that with Time, you don't have to spend successes on duration.<br /> Not really a good advantage since a few successes can make an effect last for days...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is definitely a distinct advantage for a Mage who has access to Time 4, as a few extra successes not spent on duration can mean that the Effect will be more powerful in regard to other areas. And this can mean the difference that results in an Effect accomplishing a goal or an objective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:12:49-08:00","id":1289224,"title":"","content":"True, but I still think that's nit enough advantage for a lvl 4 sphere. Also, do you know more effects like those on the books? Any rote that seems to have persistent effects or efect that changes with conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}